  "label": "User projected onto the black sellout stereotype",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the overarching concept of the 'black sellout' stereotype, which is the central theme of the meme. The meme's structure, with its three panels and the top text 'year in review: 2017 black sellout of the year goes to.....', frames the user as an observer or participant in this judgmental narrative. The user is not explicitly projected onto a specific visual material, textual material, or scene entity (like Clarke Whitlock or 'ray ray trump'), but rather onto the entire conceptual framework of the meme, which is the 'black sellout' stereotype. This projection is implicit in the meme's format, which invites the user to accept or engage with the derogatory categorization.",
